              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "26159072"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Kinase involved in a D-tagatose catabolic pathway (PubMed:23524682, PubMed:26159072). Catalyzes the phosphorylation of D-tagatose-1-phosphate (Tag-1P) to D-tagatose-1,6-bisphosphate (PubMed:26159072). Can also use D-fructose-1-phosphate, with 40-fold lower catalytic efficiency, but not tagatose-6-phosphate or fructose-6-phosphate (PubMed:26159072). The substrate, which occurs in a pyranose form in solution, may undergo a change to the furanose conformation after binding to the enzyme, in order to permit phosphorylation at C-6 (PubMed:26159072)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
